        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0365" n="272" xml:id="pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.5151/431: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Argentina</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Cox</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-25T11:00:00-05:00">April 25, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Your 32 of April 23, 5 p.m. Please say to the Argentine Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs that the Department will appreciate an early reply to the requests
                    concerning the new exchange decree which the Department’s telegraphic
                    instruction No. 34, of April 16, 7 p.m., instructed you to make.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
